1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,044
GridBot Builder.

2
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,784
GridBot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,074
Lesson one.

4
00:00:04,626 --> 00:00:05,355
Introduction.

5
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,616
Education only.

6
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,489
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,009 --> 00:00:11,833
This is general information

8
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,264
and doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,164
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,883
Crypto, a digital coin, is high risk;

11
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:21,319
you could lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,839 --> 00:00:23,890
Past performance is not a reliable

13
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,588
indicator of future results.

14
00:00:26,638 --> 00:00:29,031
The prices are public historical prices

15
00:00:29,031 --> 00:00:31,209
at the end of each day, marked Example.

16
00:00:32,342 --> 00:00:34,241
No order is sent from this lesson.

17
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,139
By the end of this series you will

18
00:00:37,139 --> 00:00:38,927
understand what a grid bot does.

19
00:00:39,324 --> 00:00:41,167
It is a small program that places

20
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:42,341
these orders for you.

21
00:00:42,797 --> 00:00:44,696
You will learn when it can capture

22
00:00:44,696 --> 00:00:46,260
bounces, and where it loses.

23
00:00:46,508 --> 00:00:48,668
You will know how to plan one, test it

24
00:00:48,668 --> 00:00:50,790
on paper, run it, check it, and change

25
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:52,763
the capital you give to bots only

26
00:00:52,763 --> 00:00:54,327
under written risk rules.

27
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:56,295
This is education, not

28
00:00:56,295 --> 00:00:57,662
a promise of results.

29
00:00:58,182 --> 00:00:59,792
Price often moves sideways,

30
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:01,543
bouncing between the same top

31
00:01:01,543 --> 00:01:03,293
and bottom instead of leaving.

32
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,523
A grid is a ladder of waiting

33
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,232
orders, called limit orders,

34
00:01:07,232 --> 00:01:08,719
built for that bouncing.

35
00:01:09,239 --> 00:01:11,083
When price runs one way and stays

36
00:01:11,083 --> 00:01:13,262
there, the grid has nothing left to do.

37
00:01:13,642 --> 00:01:15,185
And if price falls through

38
00:01:15,185 --> 00:01:17,078
the bottom, coin means the crypto

39
00:01:17,078 --> 00:01:18,901
itself, and you are left holding

40
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:20,633
the coin, and it is worth less.

41
00:01:21,564 --> 00:01:22,904
By the end you will know

42
00:01:22,904 --> 00:01:24,189
what a grid bot places.

43
00:01:25,319 --> 00:01:27,190
You will see that idea

44
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:29,372
on one real path from 2023.

45
00:01:30,572 --> 00:01:31,857
You will be able to say

46
00:01:31,857 --> 00:01:33,533
the stop rule in one sentence.

47
00:01:34,487 --> 00:01:36,333
When a chart says Example, it

48
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:38,179
means a real past price used

49
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:40,025
as an example, not a forecast.

50
00:01:41,075 --> 00:01:42,317
Crypto is a digital

51
00:01:42,317 --> 00:01:43,714
asset, such as bitcoin.

52
00:01:44,234 --> 00:01:45,910
You do not need to have bought

53
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:47,195
any before this lesson.

54
00:01:47,573 --> 00:01:49,905
An exchange is the website or app where

55
00:01:49,905 --> 00:01:52,310
you swap Australian dollars for crypto,

56
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:53,913
and crypto back to dollars.

57
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:56,109
This course does not name one,

58
00:01:56,109 --> 00:01:57,785
and it does not send an order.

59
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:00,094
Cash is money you can spend.

60
00:02:00,496 --> 00:02:02,252
Here that means dollars, or

61
00:02:02,252 --> 00:02:04,008
a stablecoin, a crypto coin

62
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:05,923
built to stay at one US dollar.

63
00:02:06,443 --> 00:02:08,510
We treat it like cash in this lesson,

64
00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:10,242
but it can drop below a dollar.

65
00:02:10,671 --> 00:02:12,862
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

66
00:02:13,912 --> 00:02:16,259
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

67
00:02:16,711 --> 00:02:18,518
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

68
00:02:19,038 --> 00:02:20,789
A sell order swaps coin back

69
00:02:20,789 --> 00:02:22,844
to cash, and you can only sell coin

70
00:02:22,844 --> 00:02:24,975
you already hold, on a spot account.

71
00:02:25,495 --> 00:02:27,132
A spot account is the normal

72
00:02:27,132 --> 00:02:28,484
account on an exchange.

73
00:02:29,004 --> 00:02:30,400
You own the coin you buy,

74
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,741
and nothing is borrowed.

75
00:02:32,623 --> 00:02:34,393
A bot is software that places

76
00:02:34,393 --> 00:02:36,015
and refills orders for you.

77
00:02:36,535 --> 00:02:38,378
You start with some cash and some

78
00:02:38,378 --> 00:02:40,278
coin, so there is something to buy

79
00:02:40,278 --> 00:02:41,786
with and something to sell.

80
00:02:41,835 --> 00:02:44,187
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

81
00:02:44,187 --> 00:02:46,304
on lines below the current price

82
00:02:46,304 --> 00:02:48,421
and sell orders on lines above it,

83
00:02:48,421 --> 00:02:50,695
inside a top and a bottom you choose.

84
00:02:51,215 --> 00:02:52,891
The space between your top and

85
00:02:52,891 --> 00:02:54,679
your bottom is called the range.

86
00:02:54,772 --> 00:02:56,878
The sells need some coin, so a grid

87
00:02:56,878 --> 00:02:58,827
starts with part cash and part

88
00:02:58,827 --> 00:03:00,777
coin, and that is a description,

89
00:03:00,777 --> 00:03:02,648
not advice about what to hold.

90
00:03:03,698 --> 00:03:05,120
A limit order is an order

91
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,968
that waits at a price you choose.

92
00:03:07,488 --> 00:03:09,052
It does not chase the price.

93
00:03:09,472 --> 00:03:11,036
Chasing the price would mean

94
00:03:11,036 --> 00:03:12,488
moving the order to follow

95
00:03:12,488 --> 00:03:14,053
wherever the price has gone.

96
00:03:14,902 --> 00:03:16,977
An order fills when the price reaches

97
00:03:16,977 --> 00:03:18,709
its line and the trade happens.

98
00:03:19,170 --> 00:03:21,377
Until then, the order is only waiting.

99
00:03:22,427 --> 00:03:24,382
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

100
00:03:24,524 --> 00:03:26,870
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

101
00:03:27,146 --> 00:03:29,436
A rung is one price where an order waits.

102
00:03:29,843 --> 00:03:32,022
The gap is the space between two rungs.

103
00:03:32,311 --> 00:03:34,734
The ladder is the analogy, and the chart

104
00:03:34,734 --> 00:03:36,627
beside it is the real past path.

105
00:03:37,677 --> 00:03:39,088
The range is the top rung

106
00:03:39,088 --> 00:03:40,217
and the bottom rung.

107
00:03:40,737 --> 00:03:42,860
The levels are the rungs between them.

108
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:45,500
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

109
00:03:46,349 --> 00:03:47,969
The range is the top line and

110
00:03:47,969 --> 00:03:50,036
the bottom line, taken from the path.

111
00:03:50,515 --> 00:03:51,854
Hindsight: this range

112
00:03:51,854 --> 00:03:53,268
is drawn after the fact.

113
00:03:53,788 --> 00:03:57,793
The chart is bitcoin's real daily closing

114
00:03:57,793 --> 00:04:01,341
prices from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

115
00:04:01,861 --> 00:04:03,760
Every closing price in this window

116
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,492
stayed between those two lines.

117
00:04:06,381 --> 00:04:08,787
Six gaps of about 900 dollars each sit

118
00:04:08,787 --> 00:04:11,348
between the bottom line and the top line.

119
00:04:11,868 --> 00:04:14,095
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

120
00:04:14,095 --> 00:04:16,322
the top line minus the bottom

121
00:04:16,322 --> 00:04:17,806
line, divided by six.

122
00:04:18,326 --> 00:04:19,671
It is one step between

123
00:04:19,671 --> 00:04:21,241
lines, not the whole range.

124
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:23,599
Seven lines make those six gaps.

125
00:04:24,119 --> 00:04:25,683
The levels are the prices on

126
00:04:25,683 --> 00:04:27,583
the rungs where limit orders wait.

127
00:04:28,570 --> 00:04:29,928
Buy orders wait on lines

128
00:04:29,928 --> 00:04:31,285
below the current price.

129
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:33,761
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

130
00:04:34,242 --> 00:04:36,741
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

131
00:04:36,741 --> 00:04:39,407
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

132
00:04:39,927 --> 00:04:41,100
You choose the range,

133
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,385
the gaps and the money.

134
00:04:42,694 --> 00:04:44,147
The bot places each order.

135
00:04:45,153 --> 00:04:46,781
After a fill, the bot places

136
00:04:46,781 --> 00:04:49,076
the opposite order one rung up or down.

137
00:04:49,596 --> 00:04:51,774
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

138
00:04:52,161 --> 00:04:54,390
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

139
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:56,531
You still write the stop, and

140
00:04:56,531 --> 00:04:58,207
you act when that rule is met.

141
00:04:58,438 --> 00:05:00,449
The bot does not decide the stop for

142
00:05:00,449 --> 00:05:02,572
you unless you turned that setting on,

143
00:05:02,572 --> 00:05:04,863
and you write which one before you start.

144
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:06,938
Think of a market stall.

145
00:05:07,370 --> 00:05:09,484
The stallholder buys stock a little

146
00:05:09,484 --> 00:05:11,598
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

147
00:05:11,598 --> 00:05:13,218
and pays a fee on every sale.

148
00:05:13,669 --> 00:05:15,238
Exchanges charge a small

149
00:05:15,238 --> 00:05:16,284
fee on each trade.

150
00:05:16,804 --> 00:05:18,547
A grid can do that while price

151
00:05:18,547 --> 00:05:20,073
bounces inside the range.

152
00:05:20,593 --> 00:05:23,114
A bounce means price moves down and back

153
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:25,483
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

154
00:05:26,003 --> 00:05:28,239
One buy at a lower line and the later

155
00:05:28,239 --> 00:05:30,322
sell of that same coin is one pair.

156
00:05:30,842 --> 00:05:33,404
On these daily closing prices, the July

157
00:05:33,404 --> 00:05:36,128
to October example window finished only

158
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:38,210
three pairs, each a buy and a sell

159
00:05:38,210 --> 00:05:39,972
on lines next to each other.

160
00:05:40,492 --> 00:05:42,503
The sell line is higher, so the cash

161
00:05:42,503 --> 00:05:44,067
that comes back is more than

162
00:05:44,067 --> 00:05:46,023
the cash that left, before the fee.

163
00:05:46,316 --> 00:05:47,768
A fee is what the exchange

164
00:05:47,768 --> 00:05:49,333
charges when an order fills.

165
00:05:49,514 --> 00:05:51,804
The fees come out of what the pair makes.

166
00:05:51,866 --> 00:05:53,374
If the fees are larger than

167
00:05:53,374 --> 00:05:54,994
that, the pair keeps nothing.

168
00:05:55,167 --> 00:05:56,411
This is not a promise.

169
00:05:56,931 --> 00:05:58,735
The pair finishes only if price

170
00:05:58,735 --> 00:06:00,608
does bounce and both orders fill.

171
00:06:01,658 --> 00:06:03,029
The daily closing price

172
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:04,649
is the last price of the day.

173
00:06:05,057 --> 00:06:06,622
Crypto trades all day, so

174
00:06:06,622 --> 00:06:08,265
the day is cut at a set time.

175
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,107
This lesson uses the end of each

176
00:06:11,107 --> 00:06:13,250
UTC day, the world's standard

177
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:15,572
clock, which is 11am Sydney time

178
00:06:15,572 --> 00:06:18,162
in daylight saving, 10am otherwise.

179
00:06:18,682 --> 00:06:20,775
This is a simple candle that shows

180
00:06:20,775 --> 00:06:23,018
the day's high, low and closing price.

181
00:06:23,538 --> 00:06:25,467
Traders call it a candle because

182
00:06:25,467 --> 00:06:27,397
the full version has a thick body

183
00:06:27,397 --> 00:06:29,129
and a thin wick, like a candle.

184
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,069
Here we only need the high,

185
00:06:31,069 --> 00:06:32,745
the low and the closing price.

186
00:06:33,197 --> 00:06:36,376
This candle is 19 July 2023.

187
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:38,125
The high, the low, and

188
00:06:38,125 --> 00:06:39,870
the closing price are labelled.

189
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,049
The example is Bitcoin's public

190
00:06:43,049 --> 00:06:44,705
daily price in US dollars.

191
00:06:45,225 --> 00:06:48,402
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

192
00:06:48,402 --> 00:06:51,326
2023, every one of those days

193
00:06:51,326 --> 00:06:53,868
closed inside the range.

194
00:06:54,388 --> 00:06:56,610
The closing price crossed the seven

195
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:58,388
lines 28 times in that window.

196
00:06:58,908 --> 00:07:01,220
The count is an example, not a forecast.

197
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:03,528
We do not need to read each day.

198
00:07:03,794 --> 00:07:05,136
The shape is the lesson,

199
00:07:05,136 --> 00:07:06,550
and it is marked Example.

200
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:09,826
Worked check: 19 July

201
00:07:09,826 --> 00:07:12,906
2023 to 16 October 2023.

202
00:07:13,426 --> 00:07:14,935
The low is the bottom line.

203
00:07:15,415 --> 00:07:16,881
The high is the top line.

204
00:07:17,401 --> 00:07:19,245
Nothing on this card is an order.

205
00:07:20,208 --> 00:07:23,078
Those 28 crossings, each time the price

206
00:07:23,078 --> 00:07:25,500
crosses a line, are not 28 results.

207
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,307
A crossing only means

208
00:07:27,307 --> 00:07:29,238
the closing price moved from one

209
00:07:29,238 --> 00:07:30,803
side of a line to the other.

210
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,186
A pair is finished only when a buy

211
00:07:33,186 --> 00:07:34,826
and its later sell have both

212
00:07:34,826 --> 00:07:36,558
filled, and only after the fee.

213
00:07:37,057 --> 00:07:38,733
The price can cross many lines

214
00:07:38,733 --> 00:07:40,521
and still leave you holding coin

215
00:07:40,521 --> 00:07:42,476
if it walks out through the bottom.

216
00:07:43,012 --> 00:07:44,521
You can buy part of a coin.

217
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:48,029
Here we buy one hundredth

218
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:49,132
of a bitcoin, 0.01.

219
00:07:49,132 --> 00:07:52,394
900 dollars times 0.01 bitcoin

220
00:07:52,394 --> 00:07:54,918
is 9 dollars before fees.

221
00:07:55,438 --> 00:07:58,110
In this example a buy waiting at

222
00:07:58,110 --> 00:08:01,503
the lower of these two lines was reached

223
00:08:01,503 --> 00:08:04,689
on 17 August 2023, and the sell one line

224
00:08:04,689 --> 00:08:07,670
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

225
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:09,755
The card shows the gap, then

226
00:08:09,755 --> 00:08:11,542
the two fees, then what is left.

227
00:08:11,851 --> 00:08:15,058
Each fee is 0.1 percent of the whole

228
00:08:15,058 --> 00:08:17,932
trade, not of the profit: about 27

229
00:08:17,932 --> 00:08:20,365
cents on the 267 dollar buy

230
00:08:20,365 --> 00:08:23,571
and about 28 cents on the 276 dollar

231
00:08:23,571 --> 00:08:26,225
sell, about 54 cents together.

232
00:08:26,745 --> 00:08:28,569
That is about 8 dollars 46

233
00:08:28,569 --> 00:08:30,655
after fees, for one small pair.

234
00:08:31,175 --> 00:08:33,074
It happens only if the price comes

235
00:08:33,074 --> 00:08:34,750
back up through the sell line.

236
00:08:34,854 --> 00:08:36,362
If the price leaves through

237
00:08:36,362 --> 00:08:38,374
the bottom, you still hold the coin,

238
00:08:38,374 --> 00:08:39,938
and the pair never finishes.

239
00:08:40,130 --> 00:08:41,918
This card is not money you made.

240
00:08:42,316 --> 00:08:44,671
Past results don't predict future results.

241
00:08:51,721 --> 00:08:53,844
Now watch what you hold when the price

242
00:08:53,844 --> 00:08:55,575
leaves the range and stays out.

243
00:08:55,955 --> 00:08:57,631
Above the range the sells have

244
00:08:57,631 --> 00:08:59,419
filled and you are holding cash,

245
00:08:59,419 --> 00:09:00,871
with nothing left to sell.

246
00:09:01,193 --> 00:09:02,813
Below the range the buys have

247
00:09:02,813 --> 00:09:04,266
filled and you are holding

248
00:09:04,266 --> 00:09:05,997
coin, with nothing left to buy.

249
00:09:06,375 --> 00:09:07,767
That is why the way down

250
00:09:07,767 --> 00:09:09,525
matters most: every buy fills,

251
00:09:09,525 --> 00:09:11,284
and you are left holding coin.

252
00:09:13,334 --> 00:09:15,568
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

253
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:18,207
It triggers if a daily closing price

254
00:09:18,207 --> 00:09:20,425
is outside the range, through the top

255
00:09:20,425 --> 00:09:22,348
or the bottom, and the next daily

256
00:09:22,348 --> 00:09:24,270
closing price is still outside.

257
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:26,243
Then the idea is finished.

258
00:09:26,623 --> 00:09:28,492
You stop the bot, which cancels

259
00:09:28,492 --> 00:09:30,362
the waiting orders, and do what

260
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:32,680
you wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

261
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,182
A bot's automatic stop is a price

262
00:09:35,182 --> 00:09:36,870
that can fire during the day.

263
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:39,126
This course uses the two daily

264
00:09:39,126 --> 00:09:41,210
closing prices, unless your written

265
00:09:41,210 --> 00:09:43,277
plan says you turned on a price stop.

266
00:09:43,744 --> 00:09:45,085
This is a teaching rule,

267
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:46,263
not a recommendation.

268
00:09:46,783 --> 00:09:48,403
The stop is your written rule

269
00:09:48,403 --> 00:09:49,855
for when you stop the bot.

270
00:09:50,088 --> 00:09:52,807
On 23 October 2023 the closing price

271
00:09:52,807 --> 00:09:55,163
finished above the top line, and

272
00:09:55,163 --> 00:09:57,428
the next day was still above it.

273
00:10:02,478 --> 00:10:03,931
Through the top, the sells

274
00:10:03,931 --> 00:10:05,607
have filled and you hold cash.

275
00:10:05,716 --> 00:10:07,950
Through the bottom, the buys have filled

276
00:10:07,950 --> 00:10:10,129
and you hold coin that you bought above

277
00:10:10,129 --> 00:10:11,414
where the price is now.

278
00:10:11,773 --> 00:10:13,225
That loss can keep growing

279
00:10:13,225 --> 00:10:14,343
until the stop acts.

280
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:16,491
You stop the bot either way, then

281
00:10:16,491 --> 00:10:18,055
you follow the written rule.

282
00:10:18,165 --> 00:10:19,952
The bot does not decide the stop

283
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:21,852
unless you turned that setting on.

284
00:10:22,124 --> 00:10:23,546
EXAMPLE, made up: three

285
00:10:23,546 --> 00:10:25,125
buys fill on the way down.

286
00:10:25,645 --> 00:10:28,945
One hundredth of a bitcoin

287
00:10:28,945 --> 00:10:32,244
at 27,630 is 276 dollars 30.

288
00:10:33,929 --> 00:10:39,462
One hundredth at 26,730 is 267 dollars 30.

289
00:10:41,144 --> 00:10:46,326
One hundredth at 25,830 is 258 dollars 30.

290
00:10:47,676 --> 00:10:50,316
Together that is 801 dollars 90.

291
00:10:51,079 --> 00:10:55,286
Three buys of 0.01 is 0.03 bitcoin.

292
00:10:55,910 --> 00:10:59,096
At 24,000, that is 720 dollars.

293
00:10:59,616 --> 00:11:01,784
A little below the range, at

294
00:11:01,784 --> 00:11:03,854
a made-up price of 24,000,

295
00:11:03,854 --> 00:11:06,318
that coin is worth 720 dollars.

296
00:11:06,838 --> 00:11:08,464
You are down 81 dollars 90

297
00:11:08,464 --> 00:11:10,400
before fees, and the loss keeps

298
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:12,258
growing until your stop acts.

299
00:11:13,308 --> 00:11:14,883
A common mistake is thinking

300
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:16,392
the bot predicts the price.

301
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:17,930
It does not.

302
00:11:18,496 --> 00:11:19,278
It only waits.

303
00:11:19,648 --> 00:11:21,157
Another mistake is starting

304
00:11:21,157 --> 00:11:22,330
with no written stop.

305
00:11:22,744 --> 00:11:23,806
There is no promise

306
00:11:23,806 --> 00:11:25,258
of results in this lesson.

307
00:11:25,497 --> 00:11:26,895
Numbers marked Example

308
00:11:26,895 --> 00:11:28,782
are teaching numbers, not advice.

309
00:11:29,832 --> 00:11:32,096
Paper or demo trading is like driving

310
00:11:32,096 --> 00:11:34,068
with learner plates, or training

311
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:36,112
wheels: you practise with pretend

312
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,938
money before anything is real.

313
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:39,975
Lesson 7 shows you how.

314
00:11:41,032 --> 00:11:42,159
Steps one to six.

315
00:11:42,859 --> 00:11:44,547
This introduction is step one.

316
00:11:45,247 --> 00:11:46,308
Then what you need.

317
00:11:46,938 --> 00:11:48,466
Then exactly what a grid

318
00:11:48,466 --> 00:11:49,917
bot does, order by order.

319
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:52,033
Then market regimes.

320
00:11:52,610 --> 00:11:54,677
Then choosing grid spacing and range.

321
00:11:55,316 --> 00:11:56,923
Then entry and exit rules.

322
00:11:57,638 --> 00:11:58,938
Steps seven to eleven.

323
00:11:59,638 --> 00:12:00,722
Then a paper test.

324
00:12:01,443 --> 00:12:02,504
Then weekly checks.

325
00:12:03,241 --> 00:12:04,430
Then common mistakes.

326
00:12:05,130 --> 00:12:07,141
Then scaling up under written rules.

327
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:09,947
Then an optional wrap-up of the spot page,

328
00:12:09,947 --> 00:12:11,959
and what this course does not cover.

329
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:14,446
The next lesson is a checklist

330
00:12:14,446 --> 00:12:16,569
you write on paper, before any screen.

331
00:12:17,391 --> 00:12:19,487
In short: a grid waits, it buys lower

332
00:12:19,487 --> 00:12:21,808
and sells higher while price bounces,

333
00:12:21,808 --> 00:12:23,829
the fees come out of what the pair

334
00:12:23,829 --> 00:12:25,925
makes, and if a daily closing price

335
00:12:25,925 --> 00:12:28,171
leaves and stays out, you stop the bot

336
00:12:28,171 --> 00:12:29,968
and follow the rule you wrote.

337
00:12:31,052 --> 00:12:31,918
Check yourself.

338
00:12:32,438 --> 00:12:34,170
Why does a grid start with some

339
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,343
coin as well as cash?

340
00:12:35,506 --> 00:12:36,791
Because the sell orders

341
00:12:36,791 --> 00:12:38,300
need coin you already hold.

342
00:12:39,318 --> 00:12:42,165
In the example pair, why is the net about

343
00:12:42,165 --> 00:12:44,923
8 dollars 46 and not the full 9 dollars?

344
00:12:45,443 --> 00:12:47,008
The two fees come out first.

345
00:12:48,170 --> 00:12:49,763
Price closes above your top

346
00:12:49,763 --> 00:12:51,563
line, and the next day's closing

347
00:12:51,563 --> 00:12:52,904
price is still above it.

348
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:55,186
What do you do, and who does it?

349
00:12:55,507 --> 00:12:57,015
You stop the bot and follow

350
00:12:57,015 --> 00:12:58,915
your written rule, by hand, unless

351
00:12:58,915 --> 00:13:00,982
you turned on the bot's stop setting.

352
00:13:02,039 --> 00:13:02,789
Your turn.

353
00:13:03,235 --> 00:13:05,414
On paper, write the top and the bottom,

354
00:13:05,414 --> 00:13:06,922
one gap, and the stop rule.

355
00:13:08,025 --> 00:13:10,204
Say what you will do if a daily closing

356
00:13:10,204 --> 00:13:12,159
price leaves the range and the next

357
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:13,902
closing price is still outside.

358
00:13:14,422 --> 00:13:15,818
Pause the video and write

359
00:13:15,818 --> 00:13:17,439
your answer before you go on.

360
00:13:18,471 --> 00:13:20,538
No real order is sent in this lesson.

361
00:13:21,026 --> 00:13:22,929
Paper practice comes in Lesson

362
00:13:22,929 --> 00:13:24,539
7, and real money only after

363
00:13:24,539 --> 00:13:26,369
your written graduation rule.

364
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,895
A graduation rule is the written

365
00:13:28,895 --> 00:13:30,605
test you pass on paper first.

366
00:13:31,137 --> 00:13:32,147
You draw the idea.

367
00:13:32,667 --> 00:13:34,460
If a screen appears later, it

368
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,176
should be a copy of the page,

369
00:13:36,176 --> 00:13:37,735
and only on paper or demo.

370
00:13:38,935 --> 00:13:41,516
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

371
00:13:41,516 --> 00:13:44,372
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

372
00:13:44,892 --> 00:13:46,776
A seed phrase or private key is

373
00:13:46,776 --> 00:13:49,186
the master password to a crypto wallet.

374
00:13:49,706 --> 00:13:51,881
An API secret is a key that lets

375
00:13:51,881 --> 00:13:54,404
an app place trades on your account,

376
00:13:54,404 --> 00:13:56,841
and sometimes move money out of it.

377
00:13:57,361 --> 00:13:59,152
Never share a seed phrase,

378
00:13:59,152 --> 00:14:01,198
a private key or an API secret.

379
00:14:01,718 --> 00:14:04,009
Nobody from this course will ask for one.

380
00:14:04,915 --> 00:14:06,607
The pair, in the next lesson,

381
00:14:06,607 --> 00:14:08,222
is the two things you swap,

382
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,991
like bitcoin and US dollars.

383
00:14:11,041 --> 00:14:13,282
A grid bot places waiting buys below

384
00:14:13,282 --> 00:14:15,523
the current price and waiting sells

385
00:14:15,523 --> 00:14:17,615
above it, inside a range you choose.

386
00:14:18,815 --> 00:14:19,932
A finished pair buys

387
00:14:19,932 --> 00:14:21,217
lower and sells higher.

388
00:14:21,423 --> 00:14:23,714
The fees come out of what the pair makes.

389
00:14:23,775 --> 00:14:25,833
In the example that was about 8

390
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:28,056
dollars 46, and it is not a promise.

391
00:14:29,256 --> 00:14:30,439
Leave through the top

392
00:14:30,439 --> 00:14:31,836
and you hold mostly cash.

393
00:14:32,275 --> 00:14:33,616
Leave through the bottom

394
00:14:33,616 --> 00:14:35,012
and you hold mostly coin.

395
00:14:36,053 --> 00:14:37,957
If a daily closing price leaves

396
00:14:37,957 --> 00:14:40,153
the range and the next closing price

397
00:14:40,153 --> 00:14:42,129
is still outside, you stop the bot

398
00:14:42,129 --> 00:14:43,886
and follow the rule you wrote.

399
00:14:45,086 --> 00:14:47,321
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

400
00:14:47,710 --> 00:14:49,330
Bring your notes: your range,

401
00:14:49,330 --> 00:14:50,950
your gaps and your stop rule.

402
00:14:51,192 --> 00:14:52,414
Keep the word Example

403
00:14:52,414 --> 00:14:53,839
on every practice figure.

404
00:14:54,359 --> 00:14:56,315
Next lesson you will write the page

405
00:14:56,315 --> 00:14:58,326
of what you need, before any screen.

